<!-- Section 04 — Features Accordion | Figma: fileKey=RxueMLDFnpgheWZp4MVk7f nodeId=8:107 -->
<section data-figma-ref="8:107" class="bg-white pt-28 pb-12 sm:pt-32 sm:pb-20 lg:pt-32 lg:pb-28">
  <div class="max-w-[1232px] mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8">
    <!-- Section label -->
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-dark mb-4">The hospitality years</p>
    <div class="w-12 h-0.5 bg-accent mb-12 sm:mb-16"></div>

    <!-- 2-col grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24">
      <!-- Left: heading + accordion -->
      <div>
        <h2 data-reveal class="font-heading font-medium text-dark text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl leading-tight mb-6">
          I came ashore and landed in hospitality. I never really left.
        </h2>
        <p data-reveal="fade" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms;" class="text-gray-text mb-10">
          Twenty years with Whitbread. Started as a Regional Sales Manager, worked my way to Account Director responsible for the Punch Taverns estate, roughly 9,000 pubs across the country. Nine thousand different setups. Nine thousand different landlords, each one trying to run a business while managing suppliers, systems, and staff who may or may not turn up on a Friday night.
        </p>

        <!-- Accordion -->
        <div class="flex flex-col">
          <!-- Item 1 (open by default) -->
          <div class="border-b border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="true">
            <button
              class="w-full text-left py-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer"
              data-accordion-trigger
            >
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-dark text-lg">
                Then I stood behind the bar myself
              </span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-dark" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-gray-text text-sm leading-relaxed pb-6">
                Ran my own pubs and restaurants. And that's when everything I thought I understood about the industry got properly tested.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 2 -->
          <div class="border-b border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="false">
            <button
              class="w-full text-left py-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer"
              data-accordion-trigger
            >
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-dark text-lg">
                The question I kept hearing
              </span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-dark" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-gray-text text-sm leading-relaxed pb-6">
                From other operators, from myself, was always the same: <em>why is the technology that's supposed to make this easier making it harder?</em>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 3 -->
          <div class="border-b border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="false">
            <button
              class="w-full text-left py-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer"
              data-accordion-trigger
            >
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-dark text-lg">
                Ten years in merchant services
              </span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-dark" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-gray-text text-sm leading-relaxed pb-6">
                Showed me how the industry actually works. The cold calls. The contracts designed to confuse. The support that evaporates the moment the ink dries. Salespeople who'd never run a pub in their lives, selling systems they didn't understand to people who trusted them. I'm not that.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: placeholder image -->
      <div class="flex items-center" data-reveal="fade">
        <div class="w-full aspect-[4/3] bg-navy rounded-lg"></div>
